--TEST--
`stats` answers a `Core\Queue\Stats` whose counters are members, and not one number a caller would have to ask for five times — `rule:concurrency/queue-four-members` and `rule:concurrency/attempts-are-finite-and-a-dead-letter-is-kept`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// § 6 names what is worth watching about a queue, and the reason the counters
// arrive together rather than one member at a time is that five calls would be
// five instants: a program comparing what is waiting against what is held
// would be comparing two different queues.
var $counts = Core\Queue::stats("default");

uint $pending = $counts->pending();
uint $claimed = $counts->claimed();
uint $attempts = $counts->attempts();
uint $dead = $counts->deadLettered();
uint $buried = $counts->deadAttempts();

// And the record is the record, not the first of those counters wearing a
// class name. A `Core`-owned instance has no property a program can reach, so
// the counters had to be members — but that is a statement about how they are
// spelled, not about what the member answers.
uint $wrong = $counts;
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `uint`, found `Core\Queue\Stats`
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
